    "body": "Current Blink IDL still uses `[PassAsSpan] BufferSource` for `controlTransferOut()`, `transferOut()`, and `isochronousTransferOut()`.\n\nSo this still seems to have a fairly narrow implementation boundary: switch the WebIDL input type to the shared-buffer-capable form and audit the existing span-to-device IPC path.\n\nThis would be especially useful to benchmark with Wasm: shared Wasm memory currently requires an application-side copy before the WebUSB call, independently of whatever copy the browser/device IPC layer performs.\n",
